  41             ONBOARD ERROR-INDICATOR LED
  42             ---
  43             Hardware fallback for ECC events when the UART trace is too slow,
  44             saturated, or filtered out.  Driven directly from the main loop:
  45               ON  on any error event in the current frame (PESEC corrected
  46                   single-bit error, or PESEC uncorrectable double-bit error)
  47               OFF when a frame is processed entirely cleanly
  48          
  49             PIN: P3.4 (T0 alternate, but unused in this project so it works as a
  50             plain GPIO).  Active-low by default because most ADuC eval boards wire
  51             the LED with the anode to VCC and cathode to the pin via a series
  52             resistor.  Flip RX_LED_ACTIVE_LEVEL to 1 if your board is active-high.
  53          */
  54          sbit RX_ERROR_LED_PIN = P3^4;
