  82          /*
  83             CACHED DEBUG-MODE FLAG
  84             ---
  85             Mirrors the latched debug state.  Updated only when the host sends
  86             '~' and the decoder asks rx_debug_active() to re-sample P3.5; read
  87             by the main loop and by UART_ISR for every CRC-valid frame and every
  88             CRC mismatch respectively.
  89          
  90             Caching this in xdata instead of polling the strap pin every frame
  91             trades one xdata read (~3-5 cycles on the ADuC841 single-cycle core)
  92             for one sbit read + function call (~8-12 cycles), and -- more
  93             importantly -- makes the debug state deterministic across long
  94             bursts: it cannot accidentally flip mid-burst from noise on the
  95             strap line.
