 410          /*
 411             UART ERROR MARKER
 412             ---
 413             Compact 2-byte marker '!' + kind for ECC events:
 414               '!U'  PESEC double-error / uncorrectable, frame dropped
 415               '!d'  PESEC corrected a single data-bit error
 416               '!r'  PESEC corrected a single redundancy-bit error
 417               '!p'  PESEC corrected the overall parity bit itself
 418             The leading '!' makes the marker stand out in a stream that may
 419             otherwise contain printable payload bytes.
 420          
 421             The function itself is unconditional; the CALLER (rx_main.c) decides
 422             whether to invoke it based on the cached debug-mode strap state.
 423             In normal operation (strap floating) no markers are emitted and the
 424             payload stream is clean -- the LED on P3.4 is the always-on visual
 425             indicator that an error event occurred.
 426          
C51 COMPILER V9.60.7.0   RX_HW                                                             05/24/2026 15:37:29 PAGE 8   

 427             Non-blocking: rx_send_uart_byte() enqueues into the 128-byte TX ring
 428             drained by UART_ISR's TI handler.  If the ring is full the marker is
 429             silently dropped.
 430          */
 431          void rx_signal_error(uint8_t kind)
 432          {
 433   1          rx_send_uart_byte('!');
 434   1          rx_send_uart_byte(kind);
 435   1      }
